  "FirmwareUpdate": {
    "//": "Release 1.1.1 (built 2026-08-07 from esp32/AregVoiceMvp, canonical FQBN plus -DAREG_CONTENT_SYNC_BENCH). 1.1.0 was pushed to the live toy and rolled back (rollback_no_checkin) — 1.1.1 fixes the first-boot check-in. The facts below are INERT while Enabled=false. Full procedure: docs/ota-release-runbook.md.",
    "//Enabled": "STAYS false in the repo on purpose. Railway rebuilds from this file on every deploy, so committing true would make a routine redeploy start offering firmware to every toy that polls. Going live is an OPERATOR act, not a merge: set FirmwareUpdate__Enabled=true in the Railway environment. An offer alone still does not push — the toy only applies when an operator enqueues a firmware_update command via POST /api/internal/devices/{deviceId}/commands.",
    "Enabled": false,
    "LatestVersion": "1.1.1",
    "//MinVersion": "Informational floor surfaced to the device; not a server-side offer gate. 1.0.1 is the oldest build known to carry the OTA apply client.",
    "MinVersion": "1.0.1",
    "//BoardModel": "DELIBERATELY EMPTY for the 1.1.0 rollout. The server gate is 'configured AND != device.BoardModel -> no offer', and the live toy has BoardModel NULL in the DB (it has never sent an OTA-identity heartbeat: FirmwareReportedAt is null too). Setting 'areg-s3-n8' here therefore makes the offer SILENTLY never happen — no error, no log, just updateAvailable:false forever. Empty = offer to every board; the DEVICE still enforces its own board check against the manifest's boardModel field, which is null when this is empty. Re-pin this to areg-s3-n8 once toys actually report a board AND a second board model exists.",
    "BoardModel": "",
    "//Url": "Bare path — the device resolves it against its own backend base (ota_apply.resolve_image_url), so one value works on the bench and in prod.",
    "Url": "/api/devices/firmware-image",
    "//ImagePath": "EMPTY here on purpose: DeviceController.GetFirmwareImage requires an ABSOLUTE path, which no committed value satisfies on both Windows and Linux. The shipped file is deliberately named areg-current.bin and NOT versioned, so this env var is set ONCE and never again — a versioned name means every release needs an operator env edit, and a forgotten one serves the OLD image under the NEW manifest's sha, which the device then rejects. Railway: FirmwareUpdate__ImagePath=/app/firmware/areg-current.bin. The version of record is LatestVersion + Sha256 here, and the versioned copy under esp32/AregVoiceMvp/release/.",
    "ImagePath": "",
    "//SizeBytes": "Bytes of AregVoiceMvp.ino.bin — the APP-ONLY image. NOT AregVoiceMvp.ino.merged.bin (8 MB full-flash, cable/esptool only); serving merged.bin over OTA writes a whole flash layout into a 3 MB app slot and fails.",
    "SizeBytes": 1321280,
    "Sha256": "ccf8ab8b0b780b8c800caf4ef2308d9f41809b36876a93e2f313e717e3ae81e8",
    "//SigningKey": "SECRET — never committed. Railway env FirmwareUpdate__SigningKey. Must equal AREG_MANIFEST_HMAC_KEY compiled into the firmware that is expected to ACCEPT the update, which during a key rotation is the OLD firmware, not the new one. Empty = the device logs 'signature check SKIPPED' and applies unsigned (bench-only posture).",
    "SigningKey": "",
    "TtlSeconds": 300
  },
